The first implementation used JS_Post(...,wait=1) for original script
initialization. The original default ship script dispatches game actions
during initialization; blocking the game owner from pumping its Exec port
caused an actual deadlock. Fixed by using OOGFOSScriptInvoke for
initialization and all test-injection stages, which pumps game messages
while waiting, and always sends one DONE even on exceptions.
The initial test expectation counted five game RPCs but the actual original
script produced four; expected result corrected after verifying exact
native selectors and actions. 8 worker DONE signals, 4 routed game
actions, 4 ObjC fixture calls, 5 actions. The wrapper and transport
close cleanly. Uses original JavaScript and selector-compatible ObjC
fixture, NOT the full original Universe/ShipEntity code.
